# wt help
emulate -L zsh

cat <<'EOF'
Git Worktree Manager - centralized worktrees with lifecycle hooks

USAGE:
    wt <command> [options]

COMMANDS:
    new <branch> [-y]       Create new worktree for branch and switch to it
    spawn <branch>          Create worktree + run init hooks + launch session
                            (spawn hooks; fallback: pi in the worktree)
    switch [branch]         Switch to existing worktree (interactive without args)
    list                    List all worktrees for current project
    status                  Show git status for all worktrees
    clean [branches] [-y]   Remove worktrees, keep local branches (interactive)
    prune [-i]              Remove worktrees + local branches for deleted remotes
    help                    Show this help message

OPTIONS:
    -y, --yes               Auto-confirm all prompts (non-interactive mode)
    -i, --interactive       Confirm each worktree individually (prune)

HOOK PORTS (integration points for pi, herdr, container-sandbox, ...):
    Executable files in ~/.config/wt/hooks/<event>/ then
    <repo>/.config/wt/hooks/<event>/ run in lexical order with cwd set to the
    worktree and context env WT_EVENT WT_PROJECT WT_BRANCH WT_PATH
    WT_GIT_ROOT WORKTREES_BASE.

    create   after a worktree is created (copy .env, install deps, ...)
    init     right before a session is launched
    spawn    session LAUNCHER: the FIRST executable hook found is run and
             wins; with no hook, wt spawns pi directly in the worktree
    clean    after a worktree is removed (clean and prune); e.g. container
             teardown for pi sandbox worktrees

ALIASES:
    ws wtn wts wtl wtc wtp wtst   spawn new switch list clean prune status

WORKTREE LOCATION:
    All worktrees are stored in: ~/development/worktrees (WORKTREES_BASE)
    Format: {project-name}-{branch-name}
EOF